WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.300
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.634
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.834
Let's get to some news.
Well, this is very exciting.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.968
"Time" magazine named
our good friend Olivia Rodrigo

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.968
the 2021
Entertainer of the Year.

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:15.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.667
Now, for all the Olivia Rodrigo
fans out there,

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.167
"Time" magazine is for --

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.033
It's for people who got their
driver's license 50 years ago.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:32.767
Some TV news -- today, the new
"Sex and the City" series

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.734
premiered on HBO Max.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.701
Wow. That's good.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.400
Meanwhile, Netflix just released
a true-crime documentary

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.200
called
"What Happened to Samantha?"

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:47.567
That's right. Carrie, Miranda,
and Charlotte are back,

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.267
but, unfortunately,
Samantha's not there

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.200
because of supply-chain issues.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.634
The first episode
addressed the pandemic,

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.767
and you can tell
it had an effect on Carrie

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.367
'cause now her shoe closet's
just filled with Crocs.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.334
So much has changed
since the show's first run.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:05.968
Between the finale and now,

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.567
Michael Strahan went from
football player to astronaut.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.601
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.033
Oh, and get this, guys.
You hear about this?

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.400
Tinder is rolling out
a new feature that will let you

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.601
hear someone's anthem song
before you swipe left or right.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:19.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:23.033
It's supposed to be the song
that describes you best.

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:25.000
So it's a little concerning
when you hear...

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.267
-♪ I'm a creep ♪

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.834
♪ I'm a winner ♪

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.100
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.501
-But, also,
if you don't like the song,

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:36.501
then you'll be swiping...

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.133
-♪ To the left, to the left ♪

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:43.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.634
Yep, women are like,
"Yeah, this is great,

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:48.801
but I'd rather hear why he's 40
and still living at home."

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.767
Well, I saw that
a man in London is selling

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:55.467
an ugly Christmas sweater
made from silk, gold thread,

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:59.033
diamonds, and crystals
for about $40,000.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.701
Here it is.
Here's a photo of it.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.300
Yeah.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.200
Yeah, usually if you're spending
40 grand on something,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.667
you don't want it
to have the word "ugly"

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:06.934
in the title, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.300
It's like,
"Here's my ugly Ferrari."

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.701
[ Laughter ]
It's the only thing

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:12.367
worth 40 grand that you don't
have to worry about

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:14.734
anyone stealing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.868
It actually took the guy
3,000 hours to make.

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.601
Yep. People are trying to decide
if the sweater

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.234
is a bigger waste
of time or money.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:24.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.801
Hey, I read that New York City
postal workers

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.400
have been accused of stealing
credit cards from the mail

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.100
and spending nearly a million
dollars on luxury items.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.400
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.968
That explains why the mailman
tipped me for Christmas.

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.467
I was wondering.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:38.901
I knew something was up
when my mailman

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:40.300
showed up at my house
wearing a jet pack

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.200
and that ugly Christmas sweater.
I go...

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.300
And finally,
a woman is suing Heineken

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.334
because she says their
alcohol-free beer

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:52.167
contains .03% alcohol.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:55.133
Yep. She was like,
"I drank 200 of these, and..."

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.534
"...totally embarrassed myself
at work."

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
We have a great show!

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.067
Guys, we have a big announcement
for tomorrow night's show.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:07.934
The 46th President
of the United States

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.234
joins me for his first
late-night appearance

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:11.601
since taking office.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.200
President Joe Biden is on
"The Tonight Show"

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.100
tomorrow night!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.934
Wow!

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.567
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.868
But first, what a show
we have for you tonight.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:26.133
They are the host of
"Miley's New Year's Eve Party,"

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.834
hosted by Miley Cyrus
and Pete Davidson,

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.267
which airs, live,
starting at 10:30 p.m.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.367
New Year's Eve on NBC
and Peacock,

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:36.200
Miley Cyrus and Pete Davidson
are here.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love both of them.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:42.567
-We're gonna talk to them.
And then, later in the show,

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:45.000
Miley is performing
with The Roots.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, a special song for us.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.100
-I love them.
-I love them.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.100
Plus, he stars in the new movie,
"The Matrix Resurrections,"

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.534
which is in theaters
and on HBO Max December 22nd.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:59.868
Yahya Abdul-Mateen II
is here tonight.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.434
Got to choose.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.434
He's awesome.
It's great.

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:08.400
Guys, we have exactly
seven shows left

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.601
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.601
for that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:15.734
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters."

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:16.968
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.100
-♪ 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:24.167
♪ 7 days left ♪

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:26.300
-That's right.
Every show between

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.701
now and Christmas,
we'll be giving

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:31.300
one lucky audience member
an iconic Christmas sweater

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.234
from the "Countdown
to Christmas" cabinet.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:39.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.467
I'm not saying
it's worth $40,000,

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.868
but it's pretty awesome.

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:45.267
Since there
are seven shows left,

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:48.534
let's open door number 7.

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:50.200
You ready for this, pal?
-I'm ready.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.367
-Let's do it.

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:53.133
[ Drum roll ]

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.734
Oh, no, wow!
-Oh!

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:56.467
♪♪

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.968
[ Cheers and applause,
audience groans ]

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:02.133
[ Band plays off-key ]

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.133
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:11.000
♪♪

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.801
Uh, wow.

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:14.501
That's beautiful, that one.
Uh...

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.467
Is there something on the back?

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:19.234
-Oh, yeah.
-Oh, another one.

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:20.434
Another little
scary something --

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:23.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
At least he's happy.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:24.367
All right, at least he's happy.

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:26.300
[ Applause ]

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.767
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:28.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:31.067
You have to take the sweater
if you get it.

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:32.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.934
Everyone, look at
your seat number, please.

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.501
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.534
Quest, can I get a drum roll,
please?

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:42.367
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:45.167
Here we go.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.634
Seat number 126.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:50.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:51.667
There you go!
Come on down!

00:05:51.667 --> 00:06:00.534
♪♪

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.467
Hi! Welcome!

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:05.968
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:08.567
Seat number 126.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.801
What is your name?
-I'm Ali.

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.067
-Ali, where are you from?

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:14.834
-I'm from Virginia,
but I live in New York now.

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.434
-Oh, you're in New York
right now.

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
Well, today --

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.234
today, especially,
it got really cold out.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.701
I thought it felt very wintry.

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:24.601
You don't have anything
like that at home, do you?

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:26.434
-No.
This is my first one of these.

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:27.701
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:27.701 --> 00:06:29.234
Here's the good news --
it goes with everything.

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:30.667
-Oh, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:32.868
-Would you like to try it on?
-I would love to try it on.

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:34.100
-Yeah, I'm sure.
Roots, can we just --

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.734
I think it'll be perfect.

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:36.934
Yeah, you throw it on your --
-Are you good?

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:39.067
-Yeah.
There's no wrong way to wear it.

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:40.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.601
I'm not sure
if there's a right way, either.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.667
-This is good.
-Oh, I can --

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.868
I can already feel
this is gonna work out.

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:49.300
Wait.
You make it look -- hey!

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:52.367
You make it look pretty good.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:55.234
Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about, Ali!

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:57.167
You make it look great, buddy!
I love it!

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:58.834
-Thank you!
-Congratulations once again

00:06:58.834 --> 00:07:00.467
to our winner.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.467 --> 00:07:02.667
Stick around.
We're playing "True Confessions"

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.834
with Miley Cyrus
and Pete Davidson

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:06.367
after the break.
Come on back.

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:08.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:17.300
♪♪

